    - target: {fileID: 6163876341813508865, guid: 32cf0b5af8e50674fa364e0526edb2dc, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "The Great Blue Heron (Ardea herodias) is a majestic wading bird that
        can be found gracing the Everglades' freshwater marshes and shallow coastal
        waters. Renowned for its impressive size\u2014standing over 4 feet tall with
        a wingspan that can approach 6 feet\u2014this striking bird plays a vital
        role in the ecosystem by preying on fish, amphibians, and small mammals,
        thereby helping regulate these populations. Its stately, blue-gray plumage,
        elongated neck, and long legs not only make it an iconic presence in the
        wetlands but also signal the health of these delicate habitats. Through its
        precise hunting techniques and nesting behaviors, the Great Blue Heron contributes
        to the ecological balance and overall resilience of the Everglades."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
